## 3. Current Performance Benchmarks

### Long Model (EXP-017 "S_Ultimate") — The Champion

| Metric | Value |
|--------|-------|
| Vault Accuracy | 69.4% |
| Signal Precision (Buy) | **87.2%** |
| Signal Recall (Buy) | 12.2% |
| Signal F1 (Buy) | 0.214 |
| Friction Profit Factor | **7.76** |
| Friction Win Rate | **84.4%** |
| Friction Net PnL | +$1,277,168 |

### Short Model (EXP-020 "S_Ultimate_Short")

| Metric | Value |
|--------|-------|
| Vault Accuracy | 69.5% |
| Signal Precision (Buy→Short) | **86.5%** |
| Signal Recall | 10.8% |
| At threshold 0.60: Win Rate | **70.0%** |
| At threshold 0.60: Profit Factor | **2.39** |
| At threshold 0.60: Net PnL | +$1,071,745 |

**Key observation**: Both models achieve high precision but very low recall. They are highly selective — they trade rarely but win when they do. The F1-optimal threshold (0.45) produces too many trades and destroys profitability under friction. Profitable thresholds are ≥0.45 for long, ≥0.60 for short.

